    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d618">

                <pb facs="0823" n="747" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg747"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5431/181</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Swiss Minister</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Peter</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-09">May 9, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the proposed trade
                    agreement negotiations between the American Government and the Swiss Government,
                    I have the honor to attach hereto for transmission to your Government a list of
                    products exported from the United States,<anchor n="7" xml:id="d618-f1"/> on
                    which concessions are requested by the American Government. It is understood
                    that a list of products on which concessions are desired of the United States by
                    your Government will be handed today to the American Minister at Berne by the
                    appropriate Swiss authorities.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d618-f2"/> The general
                    provisions of the proposed agreement to be suggested by the American Government
                    have already been submitted informally to you.</p>
                <p>It is my hope that following this exchange of desiderata between the two
                    Governments early discussions may take place looking to the conclusion of a
                    mutually satisfactory trade agreement.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis
                            B. Sayre</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d618-f1" n="7" xml:id="d618-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d618-f2" n="8" xml:id="d618-f2-content">
                <p>By telegram No. 20, May 10, from the Minister in Switzerland, the Department was
                    informed that the desiderata had been received by the Legation on May 9
                    (611.5431/178).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
